{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>Say to them: As I live, says HaShem, if not —.</b> Two negations in place of a positive affirmation — meaning: surely, just as you spoke in my ears when you said (Numbers 14:2) 'If only we had died in this wilderness,' and when you said (Numbers 14:3) 'Our wives and our little ones shall become plunder.' And likewise to the spies in their saying (Numbers 13:32) 'It is a land that devours its inhabitants' — all this shall come true upon you." "<b>So I shall do to you.</b> At successive times. And in this He swore that which the Psalmist testified, saying (Psalms 106:26) 'And He lifted His hand against them, to make them fall in the wilderness, and to cast their seed among the nations.' And likewise Ezekiel (20:23) in his saying: 'I also lifted My hand against them in the wilderness, to scatter them among the nations.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:39:52.163291296Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}